<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- The window the SYSTEM draws before this app draws anything.
         This is why the app used to flash black.

         The activity declared no theme at all, so a themeless NativeActivity
         got the platform default window background — opaque black — and the
         compositor showed it from the moment the window existed until the
         first vkQueuePresentKHR. On a return from the notification that gap is
         the full Vulkan surface bring-up, measured at ~333 ms on a moto g06,
         and on a cold start it also covers the font bake. None of that black
         was ours; we simply never said what colour the window should be.

         Saying it costs nothing and cannot fail: it is a system-drawn colour,
         not a splash screen, not a drawable to keep in sync with a design, and
         it is on screen for exactly as long as we are not yet drawing. The
         real fix for the DURATION is keeping the Vulkan device alive across
         surface loss; this is the fix for it being BLACK, and the two are
         independent — either is worth having without the other.

         Fullscreen parent because the app runs immersive anyway
         (enable_immersive() in android_host.cc). Matching the status and
         navigation bar colours stops them flashing their own default while the
         bars are still on their way out. -->
    <style name="MatrixPlayerTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar.Fullscreen">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/matrix_bg</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@color/matrix_bg</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@color/matrix_bg</item>
    </style>
</resources>
